          <p class="text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed pl-6">The earliest signs are sudden lethargy, refusal to eat or drink, and persistent vomiting of frothy yellow or white foam. Within 24 hours, this progresses to severe, foul-smelling diarrhea with dark red blood, severe dehydration, and subnormal body temperature. Every hour of delay drastically lowers survival.</p>
